<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement I:</strong></span></td><td><span id="cke_bm_471S" style="display: none;">&nbsp;</span>The value of wave function,&nbsp;<span class="math-tex">\(\Psi\)</span>&nbsp;depends upon the coordinates of the electron in the atom.&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement II:</strong></span></td><td>The probability of finding&nbsp;an electron at a point within an atom is proportional to the orbital wave function.&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table>
